<title>SWEDEN: P&amp;U seeks nod for incontinence drug in Europe, U.S.</title>
<headline>P&amp;U seeks nod for incontinence drug in Europe, U.S.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish/U.S. drugs company Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn on Thursday said it would initially seek approval for a new drug to treat incontinence in Europe and the U.S..  </p>
<p>&quot;The registration application applies to several markets, including Europe and the U.S.,&quot; P&amp;U spokesman Jakob Kaluski told Reuters.</p>
<p>He declined to elaborate on when the drug would be ready to launch.</p>
<p>&quot;We will give further information today after the analysts' conference which will take place in New York,&quot; Kaluski said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1008</p>
